---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="Zagros — Shared security knowledge for your team’s AI agents" description="Zagros is a self-hosted security knowledge service that gives teams and AI agents one shared reference built from authoritative security sources with preserved provenance.">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="status"><span class="dot"></span>self-hosted · shared · evidence-backed</div>
        <h1>Security evidence for people and AI agents.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Zagros helps individuals and teams investigate security questions using the same traceable security records. It collects records from established security sources and lets people and AI agents search them. Run it on your own infrastructure and verify findings against the original sources.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-art">
        <img src={`${base}zagros.png`} alt="Zagros — octopus over mountains, MCP shield" width="340" height="340" />
      </figure>
      <div class="cta-row hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${base}install/`}>Install Zagros</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}install-prompt/`}>AI install</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://codespaces.new/siamakhaz/Zagros?quickstart=1">Try live ↗</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}docs/`}>Docs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">In practice</div>
    <h2>Check a security finding against its source.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Suppose an AI assistant finds a possible vulnerability in your application. The assistant can search Zagros for related CVE records and weakness definitions, then cite the original sources in its analysis. You review the evidence and decide what applies to your system.</p>
    <p class="sub"><strong>Zagros is a reference service, not a scanner.</strong> It does not inspect your infrastructure or code by itself, confirm that a vulnerability affects your system, or automatically fix security issues.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost mono" href={`${base}demo/`}>See an investigation →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Who Zagros is for</div>
    <h2>A trusted security reference for people and their AI.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Zagros is for anyone who wants AI-assisted security work grounded in a controlled, evidence-backed source instead of relying only on model memory or independent web searches.</p>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Individuals and security practitioners</h3>
        <p>Use Zagros while researching vulnerabilities, reviewing code, or performing security audits. Give your AI access to trusted security knowledge with source provenance so findings can be checked against the underlying evidence.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Teams and organizations</h3>
        <p>Run Zagros as a shared security knowledge service for developers, security teams, AI agents, IDE assistants, and internal tools. Everyone can consult the same controlled reference when assessing code and infrastructure.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Core and Skills</div>
    <h2>Security evidence and agent guidance are separate.</h2>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Zagros Core</h3>
        <p>Run a self-hosted service that ingests supported security sources, preserves record provenance, and serves searchable evidence through MCP, CLI, and the web UI. The service does not scan or remediate systems.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Optional Zagros Skills</h3>
        <p>Install guidance for compatible AI agents on citing evidence, separating source facts from interpretation, and requesting approval before changes. Skills do not enforce server authorization or replace an investigator's judgment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="sub">Core works without Skills. Zagros does not provide application-level user authentication; for shared or remote access, provide authentication and authorization at a protected gateway.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}docs/skill-contract/`}>Skill Contract</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}docs/deployment/`}>Deployment security</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Why Zagros</div>
    <h2>One trusted reference. Shared across your team.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Instead of every AI agent searching independently or relying only on model memory, connect them to the same team-controlled security knowledge service.</p>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Team controlled</h3>
        <p>Run Zagros on infrastructure you control and decide how your team reaches it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Authoritative sources</h3>
        <p>Build the shared reference from established security sources such as CVE, MITRE, and OWASP.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Made for AI</h3>
        <p>Connect compatible agents and internal tools through MCP so they can retrieve the same evidence consistently.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Evidence with provenance</h3>
        <p>Keep source information attached to retrieved records so investigators can trace claims to upstream sources. Provenance does not independently certify source accuracy or make stored evidence tamper-proof.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">How it works</div>
    <h2>Sources in. Shared evidence out.</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><div class="n">1</div><div><h3>Collect trusted security knowledge</h3><p>Zagros ingests supported security sources into a team-controlled store.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">2</div><div><h3>Keep one shared reference</h3><p>Your team operates one Zagros service instead of maintaining separate knowledge copies for every agent or tool.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">3</div><div><h3>Connect the tools your team already uses</h3><p>AI agents, IDE integrations, and internal applications can query Zagros through MCP, CLI, or the web interface.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Self-hosted</div>
    <h2>Your infrastructure. Your access boundary.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Zagros supports local use, but its primary deployment model is a shared internal service. Keep HelixDB private and place shared MCP/UI access behind your organization’s authenticated gateway, reverse proxy, VPN, or zero-trust network.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start">
      <a class="btn btn-primary mono" href={`${base}install/`}>Install Zagros →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost mono" href={`${base}docs/deployment/`}>Deployment guide →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">For AI agents</div>
    <h2>One shared reference for many agents.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Zagros exposes its security knowledge through MCP so multiple agents can retrieve evidence from the same controlled corpus. Zagros provides retrieval and provenance; the consuming agent remains responsible for interpretation and recommendations.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start">
      <a class="btn btn-primary mono" href={`${base}install-prompt/`}>AI install →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost mono" href={`${base}docs/mcp/`}>MCP reference →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost mono" href={`${base}demo/`}>See the demo →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>
